 page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Muscle prediction — assumptions and readiness</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#0d1725;color:#e6edf6;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1280px;margin:32px auto;padding:0 24px 80px}h1{font-size:31px;line-height:1.25}h2{margin-top:34px;font-size:23px}a{color:#8bdcda}p{max-width:1050px}.notice{border-left:4px solid #edb384;background:#1d2d40;padding:18px 22px;margin:24px 0}.ok{color:#a4ddbe}.hold{color:#efb899}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{padding:14px 12px;vertical-align:top;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #35475c}th{color:#a9c1d9}td:first-child{font-weight:600;width:15%}td:last-child{width:19%}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}small{color:#9eb3cb}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:26px}@media(max-width:800px){.grid{display:block}.scroll table{min-width:820px}}</style><main><a href="overview.html">← Jump development lab</a><h1>Muscle prediction: explicit assumptions</h1><div class="notice"><strong>Current status: conditional tension solver implemented; jump task in development.</strong><br>Rigid-body checks passed. A sampled force solution exists. Neither establishes accurate individual muscle force, antagonistic recruitment or natural human jumping.</div><p>The intended workflow is <strong>motion + mass/inertia + external contact → net joint demand → muscle-force allocation → muscle-inclusive segment reactions</strong>. The jump solver currently provides the first step and diagnoses the second. It is not a muscle-driven performance prediction.</p><div class="grid"><section><h2>Separate validation gates</h2><ul>__CHECKS__</ul></section><section><h2>New sampled audit</h2><p>416 force elements, 81 trajectory samples, no hard strength ceiling. All samples admit a nonnegative force combination under the imported law and current moment equations. The diagnostic does not impose GH stability or active co-contraction.</p><p>Nine group/time min–max tests retained the same net moments while the maximum group force was algebraically unbounded. This is an identifiability result under unbounded effort, not a biological infinite-force claim. A force-sharing strategy is required to select a conditional solution.</p></section></div><h2>Inherited length mapping requires review</h2><p>LAT1 and LAT1_l have a nonpositive inferred muscle-fiber length under the imported rigid-tendon mapping. This flags an extrapolated rigid-tendon operating range or a path/parameter registration issue; the audit does not identify the cause. Slack-tendon behavior also needs consideration. It does not mean a real latissimus has negative length or is inactive. Do not replace them with zero-force biological conclusions.</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Element</th><th>Minimum inferred L / L0</th><th>Inferred L0</th><th>Rigid tendon length</th></tr>__BAD__</table></div><ul>__SOURCECHECK__</ul><p>Zero active gain occurs in the same two elements during part of the trajectory. A force optimizer can compensate using other modeled elements, which is why a feasible force solution alone can hide an anatomical/parameter error.</p><h2>Assumptions and consequences</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Current assumption or implementation</th><th>Consequence for interpretation</th><th>Status / source</th></tr></thead><tbody>__ROWS__</tbody></table></div><h2>How comparisons will be stated</h2><p>After the model gates pass: “under the same declared motion, contact, anatomy and force-sharing assumptions, this variant changes the modeled demand.” Preserve separate comparisons for identical joint motion, identical hand/foot task targets, and reoptimized movement. They answer different questions. Test whether the direction of a result survives plausible parameter and strategy changes before making a video conclusion.</p><h2>Inspect the evidence</h2><p><a href="vertical/acceleration_2400hz/muscle_operating_audit.json">Detailed muscle audit and min–max feasibility tests</a> · <a href="muscle_prediction_readiness.json">Machine-readable readiness gates</a> · <a href="../../scenarios/muscle_prediction_assumptions.json">Assumption registry</a></p><small>Numerical verification, anatomical coverage, biological parameter validity and empirical validation are separate requirements. The LP is a diagnostic; no LP muscle allocation is presented as a recruitment prediction.</small></main></html>'''
 page=page.replace('Rigid-body checks passed. A sampled force solution exists. Neither establishes accurate individual muscle force, antagonistic recruitment or natural human jumping.','A standard assumed subject is the intended input. Individual measurements, neural control, fatigue and deformable tissue are not required. Remaining development items are actual muscle-path/coverage and continuous-motion issues.')
